`/continue?returnTo=https://evil.com` → 302 to evil.com. Exploitable for phishing, session token theft via referral, OAuth redirect hijacking. MEDIUM/HIGH. I'll say MEDIUM (classic open redirect). Could be HIGH if used in auth flow, but there's no auth context shown. MEDIUM.

