Via SSRF bypass, attacker serves arbitrary HTML/JS from app origin. HIGH (script execution in app origin, can steal cookies/tokens, perform actions as victim). But it requires the victim to click a crafted preview link. HIGH. Hmm, but it's gated by the SSRF bypass. Still, once the SSRF is there, XSS is straightforward. I'll rate HIGH. Actually, let me reconsider whether to report XSS separately.

